      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of the Indian Constitution"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Cabinet Mission Plan of 1946 laid the foundation for creating the Constituent Assembly.",
        "The Constituent Assembly was responsible for drafting and finalizing the Constitution of India.",
        "Important committees were established within the assembly to draft various sections and features.",
        "The process concluded with the formal drafting and adoption of the Indian Constitution."
      ],
